rt\nWorkshops, Seminars and Conference\nStudent Corner\nNSS\nNCC\nStudent’s Union\nStudent Satisfaction Survey\nStudents Achievement\nInternship\nScholarship\nProjects\nPlacement\nPursuance of Higher Education\nNAAC\nSSR\nNAAC Peer Team Visit\nNIRF\nUGC CARE LISTED\nPublications\n✕\nHome\nDepartment of Education\nDepartment of Education\nAbout the Department:\nThe Department of Education was introduced in Hem Chandra DevGoswami College in July, 1967 as a core subject. The Honours in Education for Bachelor degree under Dibrugarh University was commenced in 1972 with fifteen students. From that time, students of the Nitaipukhuri region have been pursuing Honours in Education continuously. Now, the department provides Honours in Education under the Choice Based Credit System offered by Dibrugarh University. There are 56 nos. students in all semesters in the 2022-23 academic session.\nMission\n1. To promote learning and knowledge for the service of society and humanity.\n2. To create a friendly environment for the all-round development of the students on an academic and personal level.\n3. To inculcate human values and social responsibility among students.\n4. To empower the students to face the challenges of the competitive world.\nVision\n• To imbibe a sense of social consciousness among the students by engaging them in various extension activities and community service/work.\n• To develop their personality so that they can find themselves fit to compete with others in the struggle for life as confident young men and women.\n• To make them understand the importance of education in modern society and spread this message among their peers in their respective fields and thereby helping in the spread of literacy.\n• To innovate and achieve excellence in teaching-learning/pedagogy, training and research extension activities, to realize regional needs from the perspective of national goals.\nFaculty Profile\nMrs. Manashi Gogoi, HOD, M.A\nAssociate Professor\nLeena Dutta, M.